# Local development secrets. Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored).
#
# The platform currently needs no secrets to run: authentication uses
# per-user passwords in D1, and there is no third-party integration.
# This file exists for the optional tuning values below and as the place
# to put secrets you add.
#
# Anything sensitive belongs here for local dev and in
# `wrangler secret put NAME` for deployed environments — never in
# wrangler.jsonc, which is committed by some deployers.

# PBKDF2-SHA256 iterations for password hashing. Also settable as a plain
# var in wrangler.jsonc; override here to test a different cost locally.

# --- Transactional email (optional) ---
#
# Needed only for password reset and email verification. Without a
# provider the platform still runs; self-hosted mode does not require
# verification. See CONFIGURATION.md.
#
# Resend. Alternatively add a Cloudflare `send_email` binding in
# wrangler.jsonc and leave this unset.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_your_key_here

# Sender address, and the canonical origin used to build links in
# emails. PUBLIC_BASE_URL is never derived from the Host header.
# EMAIL_FROM=noreply@yourdomain.com
# PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://your-worker.workers.dev

# Override the per-mode default (hosted: true, self-hosted: false).
# EMAIL_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED=false
